27. What is retry in Jenkins?
Retry in Jenkins is a Pipeline feature used to automatically 
re-run a block of code if it fails, instead of failing the build immediately.

Helps handle temporary issues like:
Network failures
Docker pull issues
Dependency download errors
Intermittent test failures

retry(N) {
   // steps to execute
}


28. What is timeout in Jenkins?
Timeout in Jenkins is used to stop a stage or step if it takes longer than a 
specified time, preventing the pipeline from running indefinitely.    

timeout → “Fail the build if it runs too long”
Protects pipelines from:
-- Hanging processes
-- Infinite loops
-- Slow or stuck deployments


29. What is stash and unstash?
