✅ How Deployment Time Can Be Reduced (Real-Time Answer)
1. Automate Entire CI/CD Pipeline
Remove manual steps (build, test, deploy)
Use Jenkins pipeline → everything runs automatically
Result → saves hours of manual work


2. Use Incremental / Layered Builds (Docker)
Docker caches layers
Only changed code is rebuilt
Result → build time reduced drastically


3. Parallel Execution
Run tasks simultaneously:
Unit tests
Lint checks

Example:
Instead of 20 min → reduced to 8–10 min

4. Use Webhooks Instead of Polling
Trigger pipeline instantly on commit
No waiting time for polling cycle

5. Optimize Build Tools
Use:
Maven → skip unnecessary tests when not required
npm → use --cache
Reduce dependency download time

6. Artifact Reuse
Don’t rebuild same artifact again
Store in repository (Nexus/Artifactory)
Deploy same artifact across environments

7. Use Lightweight Agents (Docker-based agents)
Instead of heavy VM setup
Use pre-configured images with tools installed
Faster startup time

8. Reduce Pipeline Stages for Non-Prod
Skip approvals and heavy checks in DEV
Keep full flow only for PROD

9. Use Efficient Deployment Strategy
Rolling Deployment
Blue-Green Deployment
Avoid full downtime deployments

10. Cache Dependencies
Cache:
Maven .m2
npm node_modules
Avoid downloading every build

11. Use Fast Storage & Network
Jenkins on SSD
Faster artifact transfer
Improves build + deploy speed

12. Minimize Image Size
Use slim base images (like alpine)
Smaller image → faster push/pull

